# novadeck steamos-efi source pin — Valve's stage-1 chainloader (steamcl) + holo-bootconf.
#
# Source: Valve's own published source package for holo-main's steamos-efi. It is a makepkg
# source tarball, so it holds a BARE CLONE of gitlab.steamos.cloud/holo/steamos-efi (that GitLab
# needs a login; this tarball is the public route). boot/steamcl.sh verifies the sha256, clones the
# bare repo, checks out `tag`, asserts it resolves to `git_commit`, then applies
# boot/patches/steamos-efi/ in order with `patch -p1`.
# The TARBALL + its sha256 is the canonical pin; the tag/commit pair says which revision inside it.
#
# Valve builds this for x86_64 only. The patches carry the arm64 port:
#   0001 chainloader/bootload.c, util.h  EFI_STUB_ARCH 0xaa64; \EFI\steamos\grubaa64.efi paths
#   0002 configure.ac, Makefile.am       efi_cpu (arm64 -> aarch64) for gnu-efi/objcopy, TARGET_LD
#                                        so a CROSS link uses the aarch64 ld, the AS_CASE comma
#   0003 util/steamcl-install.in         removable-media bootaa64.efi from uname -m
#   0004 bootconf/config-extra.c         ftruncate return check
#
# Bumping: pick the newest steamos-efi-<ver>-<rel>.src.tar.gz under the URL's directory, take its
# sha256, set tag/git_commit from the clone, re-run boot/steamcl.sh (a patch that stops applying
# fails the build). The release string baked into steamcl.efi is derived from version+git_commit,
# so a bump changes the binary, and every device's next OTA rewrites the ESP's bootaa64.efi
# (lib-slotwrite.sh refresh_esp_stage1 — the one boot write with no A/B copy behind it). Bump
# deliberately, and HW-boot a card before tagging.
version:    20260824.1
url:        https://steamdeck-packages.steamos.cloud/archlinux-mirror/sources/holo-main/steamos-efi-20260824.1-3.src.tar.gz
